{"title": "Quant Super Practice — Mock #119", "duration_min": 20.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>In two concentric circles, the tangent of smaller circle is the chord of larger circle. Radius of the circles are (a + 7) cm and (2a + 3) cm. If the length of chord is 42 cm, then find the value of a.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2325;&#2375;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; (a + 7) &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; (2a + 3) &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 42 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; a &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["16 cm", "19 cm", "13 cm", "11 cm"], "options_hi": ["16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "19 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "13 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "11 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=152 height=138 id=\"Picture 10\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21879/image012.jpg\" ></p><p>AC = a + 7 and AB = 2a + 3</p><p>BC = 42/2 = 21 cm</p><p>In &#8710;ABC-</p><p>AB<sup>2</sup> = BC<sup>2</sup> + AC<sup>2</sup></p><p>(2a + 3)<sup>2</sup> = 21<sup>2</sup> + (a + 7)<sup>2</sup></p><p>4a<sup>2</sup> + 9 + 12a = 441 + a<sup>2</sup> + 49 + 14a</p><p>3a<sup>2</sup> -2a  -  481 = 0</p><p>3a<sup>2</sup> -39a + 37a  -  481 = 0</p><p>(13a + 37)(a  -  13) = 0</p><p>a = 13 cm, -37/13</p><p>So, a = 13 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=152 height=138 id=\"Picture 10\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21879/image012.jpg\" ></p><p>AC = a + 7 and AB = 2a + 3</p><p>BC = 42/2 = 21 cm</p><p>In &#8710;ABC-</p><p>AB<sup>2</sup> = BC<sup>2</sup> + AC<sup>2</sup></p><p>(2a + 3)<sup>2</sup> = 21<sup>2</sup> + (a + 7)<sup>2</sup></p><p>4a<sup>2</sup> + 9 + 12a = 441 + a<sup>2</sup> + 49 + 14a</p><p>3a<sup>2</sup> -2a  -  481 = 0</p><p>3a<sup>2</sup> -39a + 37a  -  481 = 0</p><p>(13a + 37)(a  -  13) = 0</p><p>a = 13 cm, -37/13</p><p>So, a = 13 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>From an external point P, two tangents PA and PB are drawn to a circle with centre O and diameter 20 mm. If PA + PB = 60 mm, then find the measure of length OP.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2352;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; P &#2360;&#2375;, &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; O &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; 20 &#2350;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; PA &#2324;&#2352; PB &#2326;&#2368;&#2306;&#2330;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; PA + PB = 60 &#2350;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; OP &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["20&radic;10 mm", "20 mm", "10&radic;10 mm", "20&radic;5 mm"], "options_hi": ["20&radic;10 &#2350;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;", "20 &#2350;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;", "10&radic;10 &#2350;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;", "20&radic;5 &#2350;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>According to the question:</p><p><img width=333 height=202 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21886/image015.png\"></p><p>PA + PB = 60 mm</p><p>PA = PB</p><p>So, PA = 60/2 = 30 mm</p><p>Radius of circle = OA = OB = 20/2 = 10 mm</p><p>Now, in &#916;OAP:</p><p>OA<sup>2</sup> + PA<sup>2</sup> = OP<sup>2</sup></p><p>10<sup>2</sup> + 30<sup>2</sup> = OP<sup>2</sup></p><p>OP<sup>2 </sup>= 1000</p><p><b>OP = 10&radic;10 mm</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the question:</p><p><img width=333 height=202 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21886/image015.png\"></p><p>PA + PB = 60 mm</p><p>PA = PB</p><p>So, PA = 60/2 = 30 mm</p><p>Radius of circle = OA = OB = 20/2 = 10 mm</p><p>Now, in &#916;OAP:</p><p>OA<sup>2</sup> + PA<sup>2</sup> = OP<sup>2</sup></p><p>10<sup>2</sup> + 30<sup>2</sup> = OP<sup>2</sup></p><p>OP<sup>2 </sup>= 1000</p><p><b>OP = 10&radic;10 mm</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>On a circle of centre O, from point B, a tangent BA is drawn that meets circle at point A. If OA = 9 cm, and AB = 12 cm, then find the length of OB.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; O &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352;, &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; B &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; BA &#2326;&#2368;&#2306;&#2330;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; A &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; OA = 9 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, &#2324;&#2352; AB = 12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, &#2340;&#2379; OB &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["18 cm", "16 cm", "21 cm", "15 cm"], "options_hi": ["18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "21 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "15 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=370 height=215 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21909/image007.png\"></p><p>We know that &#8736; OAB = 90&deg;</p><p>In &#916; OAB,</p><p>OB<sup>2</sup> = OA<sup>2</sup> + AB<sup>2</sup></p><p>OB<sup>2</sup> = 81 + 144</p><p>OB<sup>2</sup> = 225</p><p>OB = 15 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=370 height=215 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21909/image007.png\"></p><p>We know that &#8736; OAB = 90&deg;</p><p>In &#916; OAB,</p><p>OB<sup>2</sup> = OA<sup>2</sup> + AB<sup>2</sup></p><p>OB<sup>2</sup> = 81 + 144</p><p>OB<sup>2</sup> = 225</p><p>OB = 15 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The diameter of the circle in which a central angle of 50&deg; intercepts an arc of length 20 cm is -</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2313;&#2360; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 50&deg; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; 20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["108/&#960; cm", "144/&#960; cm", "216/&#960; cm", "132/&#960; cm"], "options_hi": ["108/&#960; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "144/&#960; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "216/&#960; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "132/&#960; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let diameter of the circle = 2r cm</p><p>Now,</p><p>Length of arc = 20 cm</p><p>(50&deg;/360&deg;) * 2&#960;r = 20</p><p>r = 360/5&#960;</p><p>r = 72/&#960; cm</p><p>Diameter of the circle = 2*72/&#960; = 144/&#960; cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let diameter of the circle = 2r cm</p><p>Now,</p><p>Length of arc = 20 cm</p><p>(50&deg;/360&deg;) * 2&#960;r = 20</p><p>r = 360/5&#960;</p><p>r = 72/&#960; cm</p><p>Diameter of the circle = 2*72/&#960; = 144/&#960; cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>In a circle two chords AB and CD intersect at point O. If AO = 14 cm, BO = 21 cm and CO = 15 cm. what is the length of CD?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2379; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; AB &#2324;&#2352; CD &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; O &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; AO = 14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, BO = 21 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; CO = 15 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; CD &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["38.6 cm", "35.6 cm", "40.6 cm", "34.6 cm"], "options_hi": ["38.6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "35.6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "40.6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "34.6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=190 height=172 id=\"Picture 17\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24543/image005.png\"></p><p>AO * BO = CO * DO</p><p>14 * 21 = 15 * DO</p><p>DO = 19.6 cm</p><p>CD = 15 + 19.6 = 34.6 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=190 height=172 id=\"Picture 17\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24543/image005.png\"></p><p>AO * BO = CO * DO</p><p>14 * 21 = 15 * DO</p><p>DO = 19.6 cm</p><p>CD = 15 + 19.6 = 34.6 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Two circles with centres W and V touch each other externally at point X. W is the centre of bigger circle and WV is produced to a point S. If STU is the common tangent to the circles at T and U where T is a point on the smaller circle, the ratio of radii of the circles is 9: 5 and SW = 84 cm, then what is the length of TU?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; W &#2324;&#2352; V &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; X &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2381;&#2351; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; W &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; WV &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; S &#2340;&#2325; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; STU, T &#2324;&#2352; U &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2313;&#2349;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; T &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 9: 5 &#2324;&#2352; SW = 84 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; TU &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["12&radic;5 cm", "18&radic;5 cm", "20&radic;5 cm", "16&radic;5 cm"], "options_hi": ["12&radic;5 cm", "18&radic;5 cm", "20&radic;5 cm", "16&radic;5 cm"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=376 height=136 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15951/image015.jpg\"></p><p>Radius of larger circle = 9x cm</p><p>Radius of smaller circle = 5x cm</p><p>UT = &radic;[(9x + 5x)<sup>2</sup>  -  (9x  -  5x)<sup>2</sup> ] = &radic;(196x<sup>2</sup>  -  16x<sup>2</sup>) = &radic;(180x<sup>2</sup>) = 6x&radic;5 cm</p><p>In &#8710;SVT and &#8710;SWU,</p><p>&#8736;STV = &#8736;SUW</p><p>&#8736;SVT = &#8736;SWU</p><p>Thus, &#8710;SVT ~ &#8710;SWU</p><p>VT/WU = SV/SW</p><p>=&gt; 5/9 = (84  -  14x)/84</p><p>=&gt; 84 * 5/9 = 84  -  14x</p><p>=&gt; 14x = 112/3</p><p>=&gt; x = 8/3</p><p>Hence, TU = 6&radic;5 * 8/3 = 16&radic;5 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=376 height=136 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15951/image015.jpg\"></p><p>Radius of larger circle = 9x cm</p><p>Radius of smaller circle = 5x cm</p><p>UT = &radic;[(9x + 5x)<sup>2</sup>  -  (9x  -  5x)<sup>2</sup> ] = &radic;(196x<sup>2</sup>  -  16x<sup>2</sup>) = &radic;(180x<sup>2</sup>) = 6x&radic;5 cm</p><p>In &#8710;SVT and &#8710;SWU,</p><p>&#8736;STV = &#8736;SUW</p><p>&#8736;SVT = &#8736;SWU</p><p>Thus, &#8710;SVT ~ &#8710;SWU</p><p>VT/WU = SV/SW</p><p>=&gt; 5/9 = (84  -  14x)/84</p><p>=&gt; 84 * 5/9 = 84  -  14x</p><p>=&gt; 14x = 112/3</p><p>=&gt; x = 8/3</p><p>Hence, TU = 6&radic;5 * 8/3 = 16&radic;5 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>In the adjoining figure A, B, C and D are concyclic points. Find the value of x.</p><p><img width=298 height=251 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/17991/image002.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2310;&#2360;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; A, B, C &#2324;&#2352; D &#2360;&#2350;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; x &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"298\" height=\"251\" id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/17991/image002.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["85&#730;", "105&#730;", "95&#730;", "115&#730;"], "options_hi": ["85&#730;", "105&#730;", "95&#730;", "115&#730;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>&#8736;ABC = 180&#730;- 85&#730; = 95&#730;(linear pair)</p> <p>&#8736;ADC = 180&#730;- 95&#730; = 85&#730;(opposite angles of cyclic quadrilateral)</p> <p>X = 180&#730;- 85&#730; = 95&#730;(linear pair)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>&#8736;ABC = 180&#730;- 85&#730; = 95&#730;(linear pair)</p> <p>&#8736;ADC = 180&#730;- 95&#730; = 85&#730;(opposite angles of cyclic quadrilateral)</p> <p>X = 180&#730;- 85&#730; = 95&#730;(linear pair)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>In the given figure, &#8736;AQC = 70&deg; and &#8736;BCD = 130&deg;, then what is the value of &#8736;APB?</p><p><img width=339 height=283 id=Image6 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p10052/image006.gif\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#8736;AQC = 70&deg; &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;BCD = 130&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;APB &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p><p><img width=\"339\" height=\"283\" id=\"Image6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p10052/image006.gif\"></p>", "options_en": ["10&deg;", "20&deg;", "30&deg;", "40&deg;"], "options_hi": ["10&deg;", "20&deg;", "30&deg;", "40&deg;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Since quadrilateral ABCD is cyclic.</p><p>So, &#8736;BAD = 180&deg; - &#8736;BCD = 180&deg; -130&deg;</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;BAD = 50&deg;</p><p>And in &#8710;AQD,</p><p>&#8736;ADQ = 180&deg; - &#8736;BAD - &#8736;AQD</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;ADQ = 180&deg;  -  50&deg;  -  70&deg;</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;ADQ = 60&deg;</p><p>So, &#8736;ABC = 180&deg; - &#8736;ADC</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;ABC = 180&deg;  -  60&deg;</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;ABC = 120&deg;</p><p>Thus, in &#8710;ABP,</p><p>&#8736;APB = 180 - &#8736;PAB - &#8736;PBA</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;APB = 180  -  50  -  120</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;APB = 10&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Since quadrilateral ABCD is cyclic.</p><p>So, &#8736;BAD = 180&deg; - &#8736;BCD = 180&deg; -130&deg;</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;BAD = 50&deg;</p><p>And in &#8710;AQD,</p><p>&#8736;ADQ = 180&deg; - &#8736;BAD - &#8736;AQD</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;ADQ = 180&deg;  -  50&deg;  -  70&deg;</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;ADQ = 60&deg;</p><p>So, &#8736;ABC = 180&deg; - &#8736;ADC</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;ABC = 180&deg;  -  60&deg;</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;ABC = 120&deg;</p><p>Thus, in &#8710;ABP,</p><p>&#8736;APB = 180 - &#8736;PAB - &#8736;PBA</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;APB = 180  -  50  -  120</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;APB = 10&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>In the following circle, 'O' is the centre and PA is the tangent to the circle at point A. If the diameter of the circle is 14 cm and OP is 25 cm, what is the length of the tangent?</p><p><img width=331 height=236 id=\"Picture 20\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p6824/image013.jpg\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, 'O' &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; A &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; PA &#2361;&#2376;| &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; 14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; OP = 25 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><img width=\"331\" height=\"236\" id=\"Picture 20\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p6824/image013.jpg\"></p>", "options_en": ["20 cm", "24 cm", "18 cm", "21 cm"], "options_hi": ["20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "24 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "21 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Joining O and A. OA will be perpendicular to AP</p><p><img width=380 height=270 id=\"Picture 21\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p6824/image014.jpg\"></p><p>OA = 14/2 = 7 cm</p><p>AP<sup>2</sup> = OP<sup>2</sup>  -  OA<sup>2</sup></p><p>AP<sup>2</sup> = 625  -  49</p><p>AP<sup>2</sup> = 576</p><p>AP = 24 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Joining O and A. OA will be perpendicular to AP</p><p><img width=380 height=270 id=\"Picture 21\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p6824/image014.jpg\"></p><p>OA = 14/2 = 7 cm</p><p>AP<sup>2</sup> = OP<sup>2</sup>  -  OA<sup>2</sup></p><p>AP<sup>2</sup> = 625  -  49</p><p>AP<sup>2</sup> = 576</p><p>AP = 24 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>In the given figure, X is the centre of the circle, XW &#8869; YZ and &#8736;ZYV = 32&deg;. What is the value of &#8736;YUW?</p><p><img width=188 height=175 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15951/image014.jpg\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; X &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; XW &#8869; YZ &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;ZYV = 32&deg; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#8736;YUW &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><img width=\"188\" height=\"175\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15951/image014.jpg\"></p>", "options_en": ["16&deg;", "14&deg;", "12&deg;", "18&deg;"], "options_hi": ["16&deg;", "14&deg;", "12&deg;", "18&deg;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Given, XW &#8869; YZ and &#8736;ZYV = 32&deg;</p><p>So, &#8736;XYW = &#8736;XYV - &#8736;ZYV = 90  -  32 = 58</p><p>So, in &#8710;XYW, </p><p>&#8736;YXW = 180  -  90  -  58 = 32</p><p>So, &#8736;YXU = 180  -  32 = 148</p><p>Since XU = XY = radius</p><p>Hence, &#8736;YUX = (180  -  148)/2 = 16&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given, XW &#8869; YZ and &#8736;ZYV = 32&deg;</p><p>So, &#8736;XYW = &#8736;XYV - &#8736;ZYV = 90  -  32 = 58</p><p>So, in &#8710;XYW, </p><p>&#8736;YXW = 180  -  90  -  58 = 32</p><p>So, &#8736;YXU = 180  -  32 = 148</p><p>Since XU = XY = radius</p><p>Hence, &#8736;YUX = (180  -  148)/2 = 16&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>In the given figure, ABCD is a cyclic quadrilateral with centre O, and &#8736;BDC = 110&deg;. Find the measure of &#8736;ABC.</p><p><img width=235 height=209 id=\"Picture 15\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21879/image016.jpg\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2330;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, ABCD &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; O &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;BDC = 110&deg; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#8736;ABC &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"235\" height=\"209\" id=\"Picture 15\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21879/image016.jpg\"></p>", "options_en": ["20&deg;", "36&deg;", "25&deg;", "52&deg;"], "options_hi": ["20&deg;", "36&deg;", "25&deg;", "52&deg;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=208 height=182 id=\"Picture 17\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21879/image017.jpg\"></p><p>&#8736;BDC = 110&deg;</p><p>&#8736;BAC = 180&deg; - 110&deg; = 70&deg;</p><p>&#8736;ACB = 90&deg;</p><p>&#8736;ABC = 180&deg; - 70&deg; - 90&deg; = 20&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=208 height=182 id=\"Picture 17\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21879/image017.jpg\"></p><p>&#8736;BDC = 110&deg;</p><p>&#8736;BAC = 180&deg; - 110&deg; = 70&deg;</p><p>&#8736;ACB = 90&deg;</p><p>&#8736;ABC = 180&deg; - 70&deg; - 90&deg; = 20&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The radii of two circles are r and R and the distance between their centres is C. Find the number of common tangents between these two circles, if C = r + R.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; r &#2324;&#2352; R &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; C &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; C = r + R &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2344; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2313;&#2349;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["4", "2", "1", "3"], "options_hi": ["4", "2", "1", "3"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Distance between centres = sum of radii. So, we can say that circles are touching each other externally and, in this case, number of common tangents will be 3.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Distance between centres = sum of radii. So, we can say that circles are touching each other externally and, in this case, number of common tangents will be 3.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>In the given figure, PQ, QS and ST are three tangents to the circle. If QS = 28 cm and ST = 3PQ/4, then find the sum of length of RS and ST.</p><p><img width=167 height=171 id=image2.png src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22741/image015.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, PQ, QS &#2324;&#2352; ST &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; QS = 28 cm &#2324;&#2352; ST = 3PQ/4 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; RS &#2324;&#2352; ST &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"167\" height=\"171\" id=\"image2.png\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22741/image015.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["20 cm", "18 cm", "12 cm", "24 cm"], "options_hi": ["20 cm", "18 cm", "12 cm", "24 cm"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=180 height=184 id=image5.png src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22741/image016.png\"></p><p>QS = 28 cm and ST = 3PQ/4</p><p>and PQ = QR and RS = ST</p><p>QR + SR = 28</p><p>So, PQ + ST = 28</p><p>PQ + 3PQ/4 = 28</p><p>PQ = 16 cm</p><p>ST = 16*3/4 = 12 cm</p><p>&#8757; RS + ST = 12 + 12 = 24 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=180 height=184 id=image5.png src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22741/image016.png\"></p><p>QS = 28 cm and ST = 3PQ/4</p><p>and PQ = QR and RS = ST</p><p>QR + SR = 28</p><p>So, PQ + ST = 28</p><p>PQ + 3PQ/4 = 28</p><p>PQ = 16 cm</p><p>ST = 16*3/4 = 12 cm</p><p>&#8757; RS + ST = 12 + 12 = 24 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>In a circle, PQ is a chord which produced to X such that XY is the tangent to the circle from point X. If XY = 6.5 cm and XQ = 2.5 cm, then find the value of PQ.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; PQ &#2319;&#2325; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2375; X &#2340;&#2325; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2397;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; XY, &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; X &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; XY = 6.5 cm &#2324;&#2352; XQ = 2.5 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; PQ &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["14.4 cm", "1.69 cm", "1.44 cm", "16.9 cm"], "options_hi": ["14.4 cm", "1.69 cm", "1.44 cm", "16.9 cm"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=216 height=119 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19481/image002.jpg\"></p><p>Here, XP * XQ = XY<sup>2</sup></p><p>XP * 2.5 = 6.5 * 6.5</p><p>Then, XP = 16.9 cm</p><p>Therefore, PQ = XP - XQ = 16.9  -  2.5 = 14.4 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=216 height=119 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19481/image002.jpg\"></p><p>Here, XP * XQ = XY<sup>2</sup></p><p>XP * 2.5 = 6.5 * 6.5</p><p>Then, XP = 16.9 cm</p><p>Therefore, PQ = XP - XQ = 16.9  -  2.5 = 14.4 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Consider the following figure, P and Q are the centres of circles.</p><p><img width=232 height=175 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20435/image036.png\"></p><p>If AB = 8&radic;3 cm, and PQ = r cm, then find the value of PM.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;, P &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"232\" height=\"175\" id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20435/image036.png\"></p><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; AB = 8&radic;3 cm &#2324;&#2352; PQ = r cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; PM &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["4 cm", "12 cm", "16 cm", "8 cm"], "options_hi": ["4 cm", "12 cm", "16 cm", "8 cm"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=220 height=171 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20435/image037.png\"></p><p>AM = AB/2 = 4&radic;3.</p><p>In &#916; PAM,</p><p>PA<sup>2</sup> = AM<sup>2</sup> + PM<sup>2</sup></p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = (4&radic;3)<sup>2</sup> + (r/2)<sup>2</sup> [PA = PQ = radius]</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 48 + r<sup>2</sup>/4</p><p>3r<sup>2</sup>/4 = 48</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 64</p><p>r = 8 cm</p><p>Hence, PM = 8/2 = 4 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=220 height=171 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20435/image037.png\"></p><p>AM = AB/2 = 4&radic;3.</p><p>In &#916; PAM,</p><p>PA<sup>2</sup> = AM<sup>2</sup> + PM<sup>2</sup></p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = (4&radic;3)<sup>2</sup> + (r/2)<sup>2</sup> [PA = PQ = radius]</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 48 + r<sup>2</sup>/4</p><p>3r<sup>2</sup>/4 = 48</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 64</p><p>r = 8 cm</p><p>Hence, PM = 8/2 = 4 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;The radius of a circle is R cm, center is O, and length of arc AB is M. If M = ( <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>3R", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; R &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; O, &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2366;&#2346; AB &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; M &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; M = ( <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>3R", "options_en": ["3R<sup>2</sup>", "0.75R<sup>2</sup>", "1.5R<sup>2</sup>", "R<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["3R<sup>2</sup>", "0.75R<sup>2</sup>", "1.5R<sup>2</sup>", "R<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Area of sector = (1/2) * arclength * radius</p><p>= (1/2) * (3R/2) * R</p><p>= (3/4) * R<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 0.75R<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Area of sector = (1/2) * arclength * radius</p><p>= (1/2) * (3R/2) * R</p><p>= (3/4) * R<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 0.75R<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The half of the length of the common chord of two intersecting circles is 16 cm. If the radii of the circles are 8&radic;5 cm and 20 cm, then the distance between the centres (in cm) is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2313;&#2349;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366; 16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; 8&radic;5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2375;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["20 cm", "18 cm", "24 cm", "16 cm"], "options_hi": ["20 cm", "18 cm", "24 cm", "16 cm"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=199 height=129 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image032.png\"></p><p>Given that MN = 16 cm, AM = 8&radic;5 cm, and BM = 20 cm</p><p>In &#916; AMN,</p><p><img width=132 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image033.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image034.png\"></p><p><img width=115 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image035.png\"></p><p>In &#916; BMN,</p><p><img width=121 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image036.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image037.png\"></p><p><img width=129 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image038.png\"></p><p><img width=288 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image039.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=199 height=129 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image032.png\"></p><p>Given that MN = 16 cm, AM = 8&radic;5 cm, and BM = 20 cm</p><p>In &#916; AMN,</p><p><img width=132 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image033.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image034.png\"></p><p><img width=115 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image035.png\"></p><p>In &#916; BMN,</p><p><img width=121 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image036.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image037.png\"></p><p><img width=129 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image038.png\"></p><p><img width=288 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image039.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the area (in sq. cm) of the sector of a circle whose arc length and radius are 19 cm and 10 cm.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2313;&#2360; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2306;&#2335;&#2368;&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 19 cm &#2324;&#2352; 10 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["85", "105", "95", "75"], "options_hi": ["85", "105", "95", "75"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Area of sector = (1/2) * radius * arc length</p><p>= (1/2) * 10 * 19</p><p>= 95 sq. cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Area of sector = (1/2) * radius * arc length</p><p>= (1/2) * 10 * 19</p><p>= 95 sq. cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Length of the minutes hand of a clock is 15 cm. Find out the total distance travelled by the minutes hand of the clock in 12 min?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2369;&#2312; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 15 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2328;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2360;&#2369;&#2312; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; 12 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["4&pi;  cm", "5&pi;  cm", "6&pi;  cm", "8&pi;  cm"], "options_hi": ["4&#960; cm", "5&#960; cm", "6&#960; cm", "8&#960; cm"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>As we know that perimeter of the circle = 2&pi;R</p><p>According to the question, R = 15 cm</p><p>Since minute hand travels one complete circle in 60 minutes hence in 12 minutes it will travel 1/5<sup>th</sup> of the circle.</p><p>Hence total distance covered = 2&pi;R/5 cm = (2&pi;  X 15)/5 = 6&pi; cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>As we know that perimeter of the circle = 2&pi;R</p><p>According to the question, R = 15 cm</p><p>Since minute hand travels one complete circle in 60 minutes hence in 12 minutes it will travel 1/5<sup>th</sup> of the circle.</p><p>Hence total distance covered = 2&pi;R/5 cm = (2&pi;  X 15)/5 = 6&pi; cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>In a circle with center O, TX and TY are tangents to the circle at X and Y respectively, from an external point T. If &#8736; XOY = 108&deg;, then what is the measure of &#8736; OTY?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; O &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, TX &#2324;&#2352; TY &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2381;&#2351; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; T &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2346;&#2352; &#2326;&#2368;&#2306;&#2330;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#8736; XOY = 108&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736; OTY &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["72&deg;", "54&deg;", "36&deg;", "48&deg;"], "options_hi": ["72&deg;", "54&deg;", "36&deg;", "48&deg;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=394 height=228 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p17034/image026.jpg\" ></p><p>In &#916; OXY,</p><p>OX = OY</p><p>So, &#8736; OXY = &#8736; OYX</p><p>&#8736; OXY + &#8736; OYX + &#8736; YOX = 180</p><p>2 * &#8736; OXY = 180  -  108</p><p>&#8736; OXY = 36&deg;</p><p>We know that,</p><p>&#8736; XTY = 2 * &#8736; OXY = 2 * 36 = 72&deg;</p><p>And &#8736; OTY = &#8736; XTY/2 = 72/2 = 36&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=394 height=228 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p17034/image026.jpg\" ></p><p>In &#916; OXY,</p><p>OX = OY</p><p>So, &#8736; OXY = &#8736; OYX</p><p>&#8736; OXY + &#8736; OYX + &#8736; YOX = 180</p><p>2 * &#8736; OXY = 180  -  108</p><p>&#8736; OXY = 36&deg;</p><p>We know that,</p><p>&#8736; XTY = 2 * &#8736; OXY = 2 * 36 = 72&deg;</p><p>And &#8736; OTY = &#8736; XTY/2 = 72/2 = 36&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}]}